{"path": "frontier/sources/i79_logarithmic_girth_spectra_novelty_r3/outside/preprints/BKT-universality-for-height-and-planar-spin-fields-September-24-2026/paper.pdf.txt", "sha256": "c5e5c165b8aa8ab967f7fdb71ce6f66a662c2679cef69de3933adcc8dbbb6dcc", "count": 1, "excerpts": [[131598, "e cell radii can be chosen so small that their continuum\nprior variances under T\u03bb\u22121 are at least C0 + 2c0 for some c0 > 0, uniformly over \u03bb > 0. To see\nthis directly, center a truncated logarithm at the cell and cut it off inside a fixed surrounding\nball disjoint from the mass. Its mean over a radius-\u03b4 cell is c log(1/\u03b4) + O(1), while its gradient\nenergy is c\u2032 log(1/\u03b4) + O(1). The inverse variational principle therefore makes the cell-average\nvariance grow at least as c\u2032\u2032 a log(1/\ufffd"]]}
{"path": "frontier/campaigns/2026-10-14/fresh-arithmetic-discovery-r72/private/intro/preprints__The-mean-analytic-rank-of-quadratic-twists-of-elliptic-curves-October-6-2026__build__sections__introduction.tex", "sha256": "cf1aec3212f453073f590cb217e06a777ac5752f6f21a6dc1c97b9867c892922", "count": 1, "excerpts": [[9884, "},\nforced by the vanishing of a derivative of order \\(k\\) of the completed \\(L\\)-function.\nIts Dirichlet-series weight is obtained by exponentially smoothing\na \\(k\\)-th power of a truncated logarithm.\nNear the square root of the conductor, at lengths of order \\(X\\) for\ntwists of height \\(X\\), this weight suppresses the late terms.\nThe approximation \\((1-u)^k\\approx e^{-ku}\\) for \\(u=O(1/k)\\)\nmotivates mollification: at \\(u=\\log n/\\log X\\), the exponential\ncorresponds to a small positive shift f"]]}
